<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Quarry Loop (from Trillium Lake Sno-Park)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:146-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.285259" lon="-121.727970"><ele>1156.8</ele><name>Trillium Lake Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:trillium-lake-sno-park (OSM parking way/148019331); confidence: high; pdf_page: 143; book_elev_ft: 3830</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.270150" lon="-121.732900"><ele>1103.9</ele><name>Mud Creek Ridge road junction</name><desc>source: USFS road 2656000: the vertex where the Mud Creek Ridge road (the east side of the 2656 loop) leaves the lakeshore road, 0.4 mi south of the campground junction as on map 33; confidence: high; pdf_page: 148; quote: From the campground junction east of Trillium Lake, ski up the Mud Creek Ridge road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.250200" lon="-121.741300"><ele>1188.3</ele><name>Top of the narrow clearcut (Quarry Connector)</name><desc>source: East end of USFS SNO-763 'Quarry Connector Nordic' on the Mud Creek Ridge road; DEM about 3,890 ft. The road's sweeping turn (Jefferson Viewpoint) is about 0.4 mi on, not 250 yd; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 148; quote: to a long, narrow clearcut below the road about 250 yards before reaching the Jefferson Viewpoint. Descend the moderate slopes of the narrow clearcut to the top of the quarry.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.249100" lon="-121.747000"><ele>1113.4</ele><name>Top of the quarry</name><desc>source: West end of the first piece of SNO-763 where it meets the quarry road 2656955 (Tamarack Quarry); DEM about 3,640 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 148; quote: Here a sharp left turn goes down a "screamer" hill (usually groomed) on a narrow road that circles the quarry.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.255020" lon="-121.751750"><ele>1086.6</ele><name>Quarry junction (Lower Ridge road)</name><desc>source: North end of the quarry road 2656955 / SNO-763 at Road 2656 (the Lower Ridge road); map 33 'Quarry Jct 3560''; DEM 3,565 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 149; book_elev_ft: 3560; quote: Ski to the bottom of the quarry, gain the Lower Ridge road and return to the Trillium Lake Loop.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.270150" lon="-121.732900"><ele>1103.9</ele><name>Mud Creek Ridge road junction (return)</name><desc>source: as above; confidence: high; pdf_page: 148</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.285259" lon="-121.727970"><ele>1156.8</ele><name>Trillium Lake Sno-Park (finish)</name><desc>source: as start; confidence: high</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Quarry Loop (from Trillium Lake Sno-Park)</name><desc>1. Trillium Lake Sno-Park -&gt; Mud Creek Ridge road junction: osm (high), 1.35 mi | 2. Mud Creek Ridge road junction -&gt; Top of the narrow clearcut (Quarry Connector): usfs-road (high), 1.53 mi | 3. Top of the narrow clearcut (Quarry Connector) -&gt; Top of the quarry: usfs-trail (medium), 0.31 mi | 4. Top of the quarry -&gt; Quarry junction (Lower Ridge road): usfs-trail (medium), 0.54 mi | 5. Quarry junction (Lower Ridge road) -&gt; Mud Creek Ridge road junction (return): osm (high), 1.51 mi | 6. Mud Creek Ridge road junction (return) -&gt; Trillium Lake Sno-Park (finish): osm (high), 1.35 mi</desc>
